AM Pipe — Media I/O for ComfyUI
================================

Portions of the OIIO read/write logic and frame-pattern handling in
am_image_read.py / am_image_write.py / _core/image_backend.py are
derived from sumitchatterjee13/nuke-nodes-comfyui:

    https://github.com/sumitchatterjee13/nuke-nodes-comfyui

Specifically: io_nodes.py read_image_oiio / write_image_oiio,
parse_frame_pattern / expand_frame_pattern / detect_sequence (the
latter rewritten as `detect_sequence_range` in `_core/sequence.py`,
backed by `os.scandir` rather than `glob.glob` for NFS performance).

The upstream pack is licensed under the MIT License (see
Z:/prod/comfy-ui/custom-nodes/nuke-nodes/LICENSE for the original
copyright notice).

This is a code-import (not a GitHub fork). Substantial reworks include:

  * OCIO 2.x ColorProcessor wired through the same code path as the
    image backend (rather than the conventional sRGB/linear arithmetic
    used upstream).
  * AM Pipe path templating via am_pipe.grammar — the artist never
    types a filename; the path is derived from the active workflow's
    metadata + per-node parameters.
  * Native file chooser shared with am-pipe-workfile-io via
    am_pipe.filechooser (extracted in Phase 2, 2026-04-26).
  * Sandbox-validated paths (rejects writes outside /_pipeline,
    /_projects).

— AM Pipe team, 2026-04-26.
